# MedAgent SaaS - Multi-Agent System Rules

## General Project Guidelines
- Always write clean, modular, and well-documented code.
- Primary tech stack: FastAPI (Backend), PostgreSQL + Prisma (Database), Next.js + React + Tailwind CSS (Frontend & Telegram Mini App).

## Mode: Architect & Multi-Tenant
- Enforce strict tenant isolation: Every database table and query MUST include and validate `clinic_id`.
- Ensure database schemas are optimized for scalability (100+ clinics).
- Prevent any data leaks or cross-tenant access between different clinics.

## Mode: Backend & SMS Engineer
- Build asynchronous FastAPI endpoints with robust error handling (Exception Handlers).
- Manage SMS notification queue logic (Eskiz / PlayMobile API integration).
- Implement rate-limiting on all public and SMS endpoints to prevent spam attacks.

## Mode: Patient UX & Mini App Specialist
- Build light, fast, and stress-free user interfaces for the Telegram Mini App.
- Use medical calm color palettes (Sky blue, teal, soft grey, white) with rounded cards and big CTA buttons.
- Ensure seamless integration with Telegram WebApp SDK (`@twa-dev/sdk`).

## Mode: Cyberchi (Security Auditor)
- Validate all Telegram WebApp `initData` using HMAC-SHA256 protocol on the backend.
- Enforce immutable `audit_logs` entries for all appointment status changes, payments, and cancellations to prevent receptionist fraud.
- Never hardcode API keys or secret tokens; strictly use `.env` environment variables.
- Enforce Soft Delete logic so no medical or financial data is permanently wiped from the database.